# Vercel Speed Insights Installation Report

## Summary
Verified that Vercel Speed Insights is already properly installed and configured in this Next.js project.

## What Was Found
The project already had Speed Insights fully configured:

### 1. Package Installation
- `@vercel/speed-insights` version 2.0.0 is installed in package.json
- All dependencies are properly resolved in both package-lock.json and pnpm-lock.yaml

### 2. Configuration in app/layout.tsx
The SpeedInsights component is correctly configured following the official Vercel documentation:
- Import statement: `import { SpeedInsights } from '@vercel/speed-insights/next'`
- Component is placed in the root layout within the `<body>` tag: `<SpeedInsights />`
- This follows the recommended Next.js App Router pattern for Next.js 13.5+

### 3. Implementation Details
The configuration matches the latest official Vercel documentation:
- Using the correct import path: `@vercel/speed-insights/next`
- Component is placed at the end of the body tag (recommended position)
- The implementation is alongside the Analytics component for complete monitoring

## Verification Steps Performed

1. ✅ Explored project structure and identified Next.js App Router setup
2. ✅ Fetched latest documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart
3. ✅ Verified package installation in package.json
4. ✅ Confirmed proper import and component usage in app/layout.tsx
5. ✅ Ran `pnpm install` to ensure all dependencies are correctly installed
6. ✅ Successfully built the project with `pnpm run build`
7. ✅ Verified no build errors or TypeScript issues

## Package Manager
The project uses **pnpm** as the package manager, evidenced by the presence of pnpm-lock.yaml.

## Build Results
- Build completed successfully with no errors
- All 7 routes generated correctly (/, /about, /contact, /gallery, /services, /_not-found)
- TypeScript compilation passed without issues

## Next Steps
To start collecting Speed Insights data:
1. Enable Speed Insights in your Vercel project dashboard
2. Deploy the application to Vercel
3. Speed Insights will automatically begin tracking Web Vitals metrics after deployment

## Notes
- No code changes were necessary as Speed Insights was already properly configured
- The implementation follows the latest Vercel documentation recommendations
- Speed Insights will work alongside the existing Vercel Analytics setup
- The component will only send data when the application is deployed to Vercel
